#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# multiple_harmonic_number

#% text
# `multiple_harmonic_number(m, [r1, ..., rk])` gives the sum over m >= n1 > n2 > ... > nk >= 1 of 1/(n1^r1 ... nk^rk).

#% text
# `multiple_harmonic_number(m, [r1, ..., rk], [s1, ..., sk])` weights each term by s1^n1 ... sk^nk.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For an integer m the value is computed by running sums from the innermost index outward, in O(k m) operations.

#% item
# With one index the value is `harmonic_number(m, r1)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
multiple_harmonic_number(10, [2, 3], [1/4, 1/6])
#% output
#= 3562366081828274275871/1207910491447571251200000

#% cell
multiple_harmonic_number(5, [1, 1])
#% output
#= 15/8

#% cell
n(multiple_harmonic_number(4, [20, 30]))
#% output
#= 9.53962023100299e-7

